# UI rules (V16–V20)

## V16 — Snapshot store, not log parsing

The dashboard must read from an in-memory `MetricsSnapshotStore` updated by `InstanceMetricsSender`.

Do not tail or parse `metrics-collector.log` for UI data.

## V17 — Non-blocking reads

API and SSE endpoints read from the store only. No collector or shell calls in controller request threads.

Store writes happen in the scheduled metrics loop — keep them fast (reference swap / copy).

## V18 — Optional UI (headless mode)

- `metrics.ui.enabled=false` must skip web controllers and static dashboard serving.
- Agent continues JSON log output and scheduling unchanged.
- Mirror the `docker.enabled` optional pattern.

## V20 — i18n (no hardcoded UI strings)

- All user-visible dashboard text uses keys from `static/locales/*.json`.
- Ship **en** and **tr** in Phase 3; add locales only with full key parity.
- Use `tool/i18n_lint.sh` before merge when touching locale files.
- Format numbers/dates with `Intl` APIs — do not hardcode locale-specific formats in strings.
- API response field names (`cpuLoad`, …) stay English — translate labels only.

## UI package boundaries

- `web/` — controllers, DTOs, snapshot store
- `resources/static/` — HTML/CSS/JS only
- No OS-specific logic in UI layer (V1)

See `docs/UI_PLAN.md` for screen layout and API design.
